@namespace DotNetCloud.Modules.Music.UI

@*
    Help content for the Music module.
*@

<div class="help-content">
    <section class="help-section">
        <h2 class="help-section-title">Overview</h2>
        <p>DotNetCloud Music lets you browse, play, and manage your music library directly from your browser. Stream your personal music collection anywhere.</p>
        <p>Use the sidebar to switch between <strong>Library</strong>, <strong>Artists</strong>, <strong>Albums</strong>, <strong>Genres</strong>, <strong>Playlists</strong>, <strong>Favorites</strong>, <strong>Recently Played</strong>, and <strong>Library Settings</strong>.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="help-section">
        <h2 class="help-section-title">Browsing Your Library</h2>
        <p>Browse your music by <strong>Artists</strong>, <strong>Albums</strong>, or <strong>Genres</strong> using the sidebar navigation. The <strong>Library</strong> home shows recommendations based on your listening history, and <strong>Recently Played</strong> lists your playback history.</p>
        <p>Use the <strong>search bar</strong> in the toolbar to find specific songs, albums, or artists.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="help-section">
        <h2 class="help-section-title">Playback</h2>
        <p>Click a song (or double-click a track row) to play it. The player at the bottom provides play/pause, previous/next track, volume control, and a progress bar.</p>
        <p><strong>Shuffle and repeat:</strong> Toggle shuffle for random playback, or cycle repeat between <strong>All</strong>, <strong>One</strong>, and <strong>Off</strong>.</p>
        <p><strong>Queue:</strong> Use the <strong>⋯</strong> menu on any track to <strong>Add to Queue</strong>.</p>
        <p><strong>Visualizer:</strong> While music is playing, click <strong>🎆 Visualizer</strong> in the toolbar to open the visualizer. Choose a preset (or load all presets), auto-cycle presets, or go fullscreen. It requires a browser with WebGL2 support.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="help-section">
        <h2 class="help-section-title">Playlists</h2>
        <p><strong>Creating playlists:</strong> Click <strong>+ New Playlist</strong>, give it a name and optional description, and mark it <strong>Public</strong> to share it with other users.</p>
        <p><strong>Editing:</strong> Open a playlist to play it, add tracks with the <strong>⋯</strong> menu (<strong>Add to playlist</strong>), remove tracks, edit, or delete it. Playlists shared by other users appear under <strong>Public Playlists</strong>.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="help-section">
        <h2 class="help-section-title">Favorites</h2>
        <p>Star (★) tracks and albums to add them to the <strong>Favorites</strong> section for quick access.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="help-section">
        <h2 class="help-section-title">Library Settings</h2>
        <p>Open <strong>Library Settings</strong> to manage your music sources (one or more Files folders scanned into the library), run <strong>Scan Now</strong> (or <strong>Cancel Scan</strong>) with live progress, and configure <strong>Metadata Enrichment</strong> — automatically fetch metadata and cover art from MusicBrainz, Cover Art Archive, and TheAudioDB, or manually fetch artist logos, all cover art, or all metadata. Resetting the collection removes indexed data only; your audio files are not affected.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="help-section">
        <h2 class="help-section-title">Tips &amp; Tricks</h2>
        <ul class="help-tips">
            <li>Use playlists to create mood-based or genre-specific listening sessions.</li>
            <li>Favorites are a quick way to access your most-played tracks.</li>
            <li>Search across your entire library to find songs instantly.</li>
        </ul>
    </section>
</div>
